// 1-26: gates, rails, and a lot of walking.
id l1-26
name 1-26 SWITCHYARD
tagline gates, rails, and a lot of walking.
bg hall
// RULES: what this room is about, how often each mechanic shows up, how hard each portion is (docs/level-design-rules.md)
main anchor yank capacitor
mechanics current:20 anchor:6 yank:4 hack:2 lift:1 capacitor:4 neon:2 white:2
new -
portion 4.2 hop 2 blocks 2 tall and 2 wide over 3-wide current
portion 6.4 hop 5 floating blocks over current (heights 11133)
portion 5.7 drive a rail 10 long, swing a 18 gap (high anchors)
portion 6.5 capacitor gate 24 tiles away
portion 6.2 hop 5 floating blocks over current (heights 21111)
portion 6 hop 5 floating blocks over current (heights 13333)
portion 5 a low ceiling 9 long over a current notch
portion 5.6 hack port opens a gate, 6-wide current beyond
portion 5 capacitor lift up through gates to the top lane
portion 5.5 a 4-tall plateau 9 wide with a current notch on top
portion 4.6 hack port opens a gate, 4-wide current beyond
portion 5.4 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 18 gap (ceiling anchors)
portion 6.5 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 26 gap (mid, ceiling anchors)
portion 6.6 drive a rail 12 long, swing a 22 gap (high, ceiling anchors)
portion 5.6 capacitor gate 18 tiles away, a block on the way
portion 7.8 capacitor gate 26 tiles away, current notch on the way
portion 6.3 neon/white stones nWnW (2 wide, 4 apart) over current
hardness 5.8
map
